# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - no Sink is registered by this module.
#
# PubSubSink used to be listed here, "pre-registered for sprint-4
# auto-config". It was removed in sprint-23 (Story 1.2) for two independent
# reasons:
#
#  1. NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE. Its only constructor takes a pre-built Publisher
#     (PubSubSink.java:58), which itself carries the topic name and the
#     batching/retry settings. ServiceLoader raised
#     ServiceConfigurationError on every discovery pass; AutoConfig
#     swallowed it before Story 1.1.
#
#  2. Sink IS NOT A ONE-PER-CLASSPATH CONTRACT. AutoConfig deliberately
#     exposes no singular sink() accessor - only the plural sinks()
#     (AutoConfig.java:268-270) - unlike warehouse(), blobStore() and
#     jobControl(). A topic is per-stage wiring, not per-environment
#     configuration, so a no-arg constructor would have to pick ONE topic
#     out of the environment and be wrong for every pipeline with two
#     outputs.
#
# Removing the line is behaviour-identical to the swallowed error it
# replaces - discovery still yields no Sink from this module - but it no
# longer advertises a lie, and it satisfies Story 1.2 AC 3.
#
# The class is unchanged and fully supported. Construct it per stage:
#     new PubSubSink(publisher)
